<name>Power Window System</name>
<para id="RM0000005DV00SX" category="J" type-id="300LY" name-id="752B8-00" from="200612">
<dtccode/>
<dtcname>Window Cannot Be Operated by Regulator Switch at Each Seat</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM0000005DV00SX_05" type-id="31" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___000024R00000">
<name>Circuit Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<ptxt>When the IG is ON and the power window regulator switch assembly (each seat) is operated, the power window regulator motor assembly (each seat) is driven. The power window regulator motor assembly (each seat) has a motor function, a regulator function and an ECU function.</ptxt>
<atten3>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>The power window system uses the Body Electronics Area Network. First, follow "How to Proceed with Troubleshooting" to perform the "communication function inspection" and confirm that there is no malfunction in the communication system before proceeding with troubleshooting.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>When the power window regulator motor assembly (each seat) is replaced with a new one, perform the power window system registration settings. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM000002FNJ005X"/>)</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten3>
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>The inspection procedure for the front passenger side is shown below. If a malfunction occurs at a seat other than the front passenger side (rear right, rear left), inspect the circuit of the relevant seat by referring to the procedure below.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM0000005DV00SX_06" type-id="32" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___000024S00000">
<name>Wiring Diagram</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="B167358J01" width="7.106578999in" height="5.787629434in"/>
</figure>
</content5>
</subpara>
